{
    "background_story": "Fernanda was a brilliant archaeologist with a passion for deciphering ancient languages. Growing up in Mexico, she was fascinated by the pictographs that adorned the walls of the Mayan ruins near her hometown. As she delved deeper into her studies, Fernanda became an expert in the field, able to interpret the intricate symbols and images that told the stories of a long-lost civilization. Her groundbreaking research on the pictographs of the Mayan calendar led to a new understanding of the culture's spiritual and astronomical practices. Fernanda's work took her to remote sites around the world, where she uncovered and documented previously unknown pictographs, shedding light on the history of human expression and communication. Her dedication to preserving these ancient stories earned her international recognition and a reputation as a leading authority in her field.",
